---
title: "withdraw_as_coin (Current Finance - Pebble Protocol Lending)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_validate: app.validate_market(market)
    q_validate --> q_version: app.ensure_version_matches()
    q_version --> q_check_circuit: assert(!market.has_circuit_break_triggered())
    q_check_circuit --> q_error: circuit break triggered
    q_check_circuit --> q_timestamp: now = clock.timestamp_ms() / 1000
    q_timestamp --> q_handle_withdraw: market.handle_withdraw(obligation_id, ctoken_to_burn, decimals_registry, x_oracle, clock, now, ctx)
    q_handle_withdraw --> q_check_health: check obligation health factor after withdrawal
    q_check_health --> q_error_undercollateral: risk level >= 1
    q_check_health --> q_burn: burn ctoken from obligation's collateral
    q_burn --> q_update_miner: miner.update_obligation_reward_manager(deposit_type, obligation_id, ctokens_remaining, clock)
    q_update_miner --> q_emit: emit WithdrawEvent
    q_emit --> [*]: return Coin (underlying asset)

    note right of q_handle_withdraw
        INV-001: Health factor must remain below 1.0 (fully collateralized) after withdrawal
        INV-002: withdraw_amount = exchange_rate * ctoken_to_burn
        INV-003: ctokens_remaining = obligation's ctoken balance after burn
    end note

    note right of q_burn
        INV-004: Oracle prices consulted to verify collateral sufficiency post-withdrawal
        INV-005: Only obligation owner (via cap) can withdraw their collateral
    end note
